  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 245 AM CDT Fri Oct 23 2026\n\nConditions are largely quiet to kick off our Friday. The area \nsits beneath clear skies while temperatures have fallen into the\n40s; still hanging out in the 50s in the city. A bank of dense \nfog crept into northern Lake Co last evening and has been very \ngradually expanding south and west. As of 2:30 AM, dense fog \ncoverage remains confined to northeastern portions of the county\nand up near then WI state line. Accordingly, we made the \ndecision to issue a Dense Fog Advisory for Lake County, IL \nthrough 9 AM. It's possible by daybreak that pockets of dense \nfog expand into portions of McHenry and northern Cook counties. \nElsewhere, several sites around the CWA are reporting 3 to 5 \nmile visibilities as dewpoint depressions continue to drop. \nOutside of the aforementioned areas, such visibilities will \nremain possible around the CWA through dawn with the primary \ndense fog concerns in our northeast, but can't rule out some \npockets of denser fog farther west and south. Any fog should \nburn off by mid- morning at the latest.\n\nSurface high pressure and low level ridge axis will slide to \nour east today bringing light southerly winds and more mostly \nsunny skies. Temperatures will again be very comfortable for \nlate October with highs forecast in the lower and middle 70s; \nmaybe stuck in the upper 60s near the lakeshore. Similar \ntemperatures are expected through the weekend with a good mix of\nclouds and sunshine. The prominent surface high will continue \nto keep the rain away as it scoots east across the Great Lakes.\n\nA cold front will work into the upper Midwest and provide some \nupstream rain chances over the weekend. However, the front \nappears to lose a lot of its luster before moving across the \narea late Sunday into Monday and the better layer moisture is \nprogged to get locked up to our north, so ultimately not \nexpecting rain in our local area early next week. This front \neven looks to lift back north across our area again as a warm \nfront in the Tuesday to Wednesday window, but again with no rain\nin the forecast. Next appreciable opportunity for rain may be \nwith the trailing cold front Thursday into Friday, but of \ncourse, much uncertainty with this. In the meantime, expect \nwarmer-than-normal conditions to continue with 60s and lower 70s\nfavored next week.\n\nDoom",
